Can&#39;t? &nbsp;I would say no. &nbsp;Given every deck was perfectly stacked, I would say that any combination of 3-5 heroes can beat any villain. &nbsp;(Even Legacy, Parse, &amp; Wraith vs the Ennead is winnable if Shu comes out last and you are very, very lucky)

&nbsp;

That said, there are some combinations that require absurd amounts of luck. &nbsp;The [url=https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/play-this-7506]Play This![/url] thread recently had trouble with AZ, AA, and Bunker vs Advanced Matriarch in Rook City. &nbsp;I retain my belief that the game is solvable (although I haven&#39;t proved it yet), but you&#39;re unlikely to see a victory in a normal game.

I &#39;beat&#39; Advanced Ennead [url=https://greaterthangames.com/comment/97129#comment-97129]here[/url] with Legacy, Parse, and Wraith. &nbsp;It&#39;s possible, although improbable. &nbsp;And all other characters can deal non-projectile non-melee damage. &nbsp;(Well, Setback can&#39;t except to himself, but he can redirect villain damage, which works just as well)

&nbsp;

I just did the math for the AZ, AA, Bunker vs Matriarch matchup mentioned above, and it&#39;s easy.

&nbsp;

Round one:<br /> Horrid Cacophony x2, Impale, Syncophated Onslaught (Bunker &amp; AZ), Flak Cannon [4], Toxic Sludge [5]. &nbsp;Matriarch at 61. 

Round two:<br /> Darken the Skies x2, ([3] from first Impale), Impale, Xu&#39;s Bell, (onslaught Bunker &amp; AZ, [1]), Grenade Launcher (cannon [4]), Second Toxic Sludge [10]. &nbsp;Matriarch at 43. 

Round three:

Carrion Fields x2, ([6] from Impales), Cold Snap, &lt;some ongoing or equipment&gt;, (onslaught Bunker &amp; AZ, [1], Turret Mode [9], Dr. Tremane ([10] from sludge). &nbsp;Matriarch at 17.

Round four: Darken the Skies, Hugin (destroy AA&#39;s extra card), [8] from AZ&#39;s start of turn, [1] from AA, [9] from Bunker. &nbsp;Matriarch is at -1.<br /><br /><br />And I didn&#39;t even bother to try complicated shenanigans with AA.<br /><br />Round four is the sweet spot for the Matriarch. &nbsp;If you deal 70 damage to her before round 5, then (as demonstrated) you can basically ignore her deck. &nbsp;Infinitor is probably going to be harder. &nbsp;
